  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Constructing The Server Routes**\n\nI\'m now focused on the `/server.ts` file. I\'m building out the API routes, specifically `/api/diet-advice`, `/api/workout-plan`, `/api/skill-challenge`, and `/api/learning`. I\'m outlining the initial structure to define the back-end functionality, intending to deliver on the endpoints.\n\n\n**Refining Model Selection**\n\nI\'ve decided to refine the approach for model selection. I\'ll stick with `gemini-3.5-flash` for its responsiveness and cost-effectiveness. The server will now handle static assets correctly in production from `dist/index.html` and uses the Vite dev server for development. I\'m focusing on crafting a robust `/server.ts` file, ensuring error handling and correct `User-Agent` setting for compliance.\n\n\n**Defining API Endpoints**\n\nI\'m now detailing the API endpoints for the Express server. The `/api/diet-advice` endpoint will accept a list of meals in the request body. My plan is to use Gemini to analyze the nutritional content and return health suggestions. I\'m focusing on structuring the response as either JSON or clean Markdown, with an emphasis on returning well-formatted JSON to allow simple parsing of different stats. I\'m considering using `Type.OBJECT` for a reliable schema to ensure 100% stable, easily parse-able JSON.\n\n\n**Structuring Response Schemas**\n\nI\'m currently focused on defining the API response schemas for `/api/diet-advice` and `/api/workout-plan` to ensure predictable data structures. I\'m leveraging `Type.OBJECT` to establish well-defined, easily parsed JSON outputs. For diet advice, I\'m including calories, macronutrients, an analysis, and a score. For workout plans, I\'m outlining warmup details, a list of exercises and the specific details of exercises.\n\n\n**Defining Workout Response Schema**\n\nI\'m now detailing the schema for workout plan responses. I\'ve structured it to include warmup details, a list of exercises with exercise name, sets, and descriptions, and cooldown tips. The goal is to provide a well-defined structure for straightforward parsing of exercise data. I\'m leveraging `Type.OBJECT` to establish this schema for a predictable JSON output.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will create the backend Express server `/server.ts` to manage API requests and use the Gemini API securely, avoiding any client-side key exposure. This handles server-side routing, static asset rendering, and JSON-structured Gemini interactions."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 7
      nanos: 821054022
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
