    thinking: "**Reviewing Project Requirements**\n\nOkay, I\'ve got a functional Express + Vite server in TypeScript! My focus is shifting to pinpointing the necessary endpoints and modifications. I\'m now reviewing the project\'s requirements to ensure everything is covered. I\'ve begun to translate the requirement for image upload with intelligent analysis and population of a \"what I ate today\" field.\n\n\n**Defining Image Analysis Endpoint**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the image analysis endpoint. I\'ve decided `/api/analyze-diet-image` is the most fitting route. I\'ve sketched out the plan for an Express router that accepts a base64 image and uses the `gemini-3.5-flash` model for analysis. The API structure is taking shape, and the code example for the AI call is now clear. I\'m focusing on parsing the request to make the AI call.\n\n\n**Structuring AI Response**\n\nOkay, I\'m now crafting the instructions and output schema for the Gemini model. I need to ensure a structured JSON response. I\'ve defined a TypeScript schema that includes the food description, suggested meal period, and a health note. I\'ve decided to refine the properties to be more precise, including `text`, `period`, and `note`. I\'m starting to consider how to track client usage limits. The client can track and manage daily intelligent camera usage.\n\n\n"
