    thinking: "**Simplifying Sleep and Workout**\n\nI\'m focusing on streamlining sleep tracking, aiming for \"one-click\" recording options. My immediate thought is to implement preset standard sleep patterns, like a common 8-hour block (23:00 - 07:00). I\'m looking at how best to translate these simplifications across both Sleep and Workout to maximize impact.\n\n\n**Implementing Quick Presets**\n\nI\'ve been working on those \"one-click\" recording options! I\'m now developing quick presets for sleep patterns and workout routines. For sleep, I am thinking of including \"Early Bird\" and \"Hard Worker\" options, to allow speedy logging. Workout presets are also in progress, such as \"Night Run\" and \"Post-Meal Walk\". This allows for lightning-fast logging! I\'m aiming for single-click functionality.\n\n\n**Designing Task Visibility**\n\nI\'m now focused on prominent task reminders within the app. I\'m visualizing alert banners for uncompleted tasks, like \"Read 20 pages\" or \"2 Weekly Tasks Pending\". My current focus is on a stylish, high-visibility widget, perhaps a soft amber alert with a pulse or glow effect, titled \"MustDoTasks\". I\'ve decided to define a `MustDoTask` interface in `/src/types.ts` to manage this data.\n\n\n**Refining Interface Aesthetics**\n\nI\'m now focused on the app\'s visual style, specifically removing the \"AI purple\" aesthetic. My current plan involves replacing all indigo and violet elements with cleaner, more modern palettes. This includes swapping the top bar\'s indigo with charcoal/slate/zinc, and replacing the header and active tab indicators. I\'m exploring emerald for nature and health aspects, and teal/amber/zinc for accenting. I\'m taking a look at `src/App.tsx` for these style elements.\n\n\n**Updating Color Palettes**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on replacing those AI-influenced colors. I\'m focusing on those gradients, specifically deep forest greens, emerald, and teal. I\'m thinking slate/charcoal for the backdrops, which will feel organic and calm. I\'m going to update `SleepSection.tsx` and the indigo elements to reflect this. I\'m aiming for a minimalist UI, with deep charcoal details, elegant negative space, and a high-contrast premium feel.\n\n**Adding Import/Export Feature**\n\nI\'ve also moved on to creating a \"Data Backup & Migration\" interface. My current plan involves adding a mechanism for data import and export within the app. I\'m still deciding on the best location for this, thinking a gear icon, a dialog box, or perhaps somewhere in the bottom panel.\n\n\n"
