    thinking: "**Updating Section Progress**\n\nI\'m thrilled with the progress on the UI overhaul! `SleepSection.tsx` and `WorkoutSection.tsx` are now much improved. I\'m focusing on `DietSection.tsx` next, aiming for a photo analysis widget. The plan is to keep it elegant and limit the feature to three uses per day.\n\n\n**Refining Image Handling**\n\nI\'ve been working on the image handling for the `DietSection.tsx`. I\'m focusing on the compression strategy now. My approach involves reading the file, loading it into an image, drawing it onto a 600x600 canvas, and generating a compressed base64 JPEG data URL. I\'m also implementing the daily usage limit of three image analyses, and displaying feedback to the user when they hit the limit, while managing state with the `sd_camera_analysis_count_v1` key in `localStorage`.\n\n\n**Analyzing AI Response**\n\nI\'m now integrating the AI response from image analysis. I parse the returned JSON to update food inputs and display a success banner with extracted details. I\'m also incrementing the analysis counter in `localStorage` and updating the date for the usage limit. Error handling is in place, displaying specific messages for failed analyses or unrecognized food. I\'m making sure to manage states to accurately capture the results.\n\n\n**Optimizing Image Processing**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on optimizing the `resizeAndBase64` function within `DietSection.tsx`. My current focus is refining the image resizing and compression logic. I\342\200\231m experimenting with different compression ratios and canvas sizes to balance image quality and file size for faster processing. I\'m also ensuring the function handles various image aspect ratios correctly while maintaining the daily analysis limit.\n\n\n"
