 situation. I\'ve designed a custom CSS block with a `marquee` keyframe, allowing the banner to smoothly scroll. The inline approach is robust and provides consistent results!\n\n\n**Enhancing Marquee Dynamics**\n\nI\'m now focusing on improving the marquee\'s functionality. The plan is to create a seamless loop by duplicating the task list if it\'s too short. This ensures the marquee scrolls continuously, no matter the content. I\'m also exploring making the tasks clickable, creating a very responsive interaction. I\'m currently working to position the home button at the center of the UI.\n\n\n**Revisiting Centralization**\n\nI\'m now revisiting the home view\'s layout, specifically the centrality of the \"Check-In\" button. My plan is to make the home layout as follows: a header, then the marquee, then a center section where the interactive button is, and then the timeline stream. I\'m exploring different layouts to make the button perfectly centered: making the button the centerpiece and keeping the timeline at the bottom, or putting the button in a central section with the marquee and the timeline. I\'m experimenting to keep the button\'s design as high-contrast and beautiful as possible.\n\n\n"
